\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reading the full assignment (
\f1\fs26 Take-Home Assessment \'97 Senior Agentic AI Engineer
\f0\fs24 , 5-day time budget) changes the picture significantly. The earlier "lightweight Supervisor + 2 Workers" sketch was optimized for a 20-minute live coding test, whereas this rubric explicitly weights 
\f2\b Agent Design (25%)
\f0\b0 , 
\f2\b Grounding & Correctness (20%)
\f0\b0 , 
\f2\b Action Quality & Guardrails (20%)
\f0\b0 , 
\f2\b Evaluation Rigor (20%)
\f0\b0 , and 
\f2\b Engineering & Communication (15%)
\f0\b0 .\
Specifically, a simple Security/Hardware split misses four explicit requirements in the PDF:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Planning & Explicit Agent Loop:
\f0\b0  The prompt states 
\f3\i "A simple prompt wrapper is insufficient. Your solution should include: Planning, Tool calling, Explicit agent loop."
\f0\i0  A basic router without a planning/verification loop will lose points on the 25% Agent Design rubric.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Action Proposals + Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) Guardrails:
\f0\b0  The agent must propose and execute state-changing tools (
\f1\fs26 create_upgrade_order
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 open_remediation_ticket
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 flag_device_for_replacement
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 notify_employee
\f0\fs24 ), enforce 
\f2\b strict 
\f4\fs26 company_id
\f2\fs24  tenant isolation
\f0\b0  at the tool/data boundary (not just in the system prompt), pause via LangGraph's 
\f1\fs26 interrupt()
\f0\fs24  for 
\f2\b explicit human approval
\f0\b0 , write immutable 
\f2\b audit logs
\f0\b0 , and 
\f2\b refuse actions without sufficient evidence
\f0\b0 .\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Grounding & Traceability:
\f0\b0  Every answer and insight must cite exact evidence (
\f1\fs26 device_id
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 collected_at
\f0\fs24 timestamps, metric values) and avoid unsupported conclusions.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Runnable Evaluation Suite (20% of grade):
\f0\b0  You need a deterministic test suite covering QA accuracy, trend detection, cross-tenant isolation rejection, and guardrail/evidence refusal cases.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

