\f2\b\fs28 \cf0 Why Each Component Directly Hits the Rubric\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 1. Data & Tenant Isolation Layer (Guardrails \'97 20%)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 In-Memory DuckDB / SQLite Loader:
\f0\b0  Loads 
\f1\fs26 device-telemetry-dataset.ndjson
\f0\fs24  into normalized tables (
\f1\fs26 snapshots
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 disk_volumes
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 installed_software
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 compliance_results
\f0\fs24 ) with derived views for trends (e.g., disk burn rate, battery capacity degradation, RAM pressure, compliance drift).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Hard Tenant Boundary (
\f4\fs26 company_id
\f2\fs24  via 
\f4\fs26 RunnableConfig
\f2\fs24 ):
\f0\b0  Never let the LLM pass 
\f1\fs26 company_id
\f0\fs24  as a free-text tool argument that it could hallucinate or be prompt-injected to bypass. Inject 
\f1\fs26 tenant_id
\f0\fs24  via LangGraph's 
\f1\fs26 config["configurable"]["tenant_id"]
\f0\fs24  (using 
\f1\fs26 InjectedToolArg
\f0\fs24 ), and automatically append 
\f1\fs26 WHERE company_id = :tenant_id
\f0\fs24  inside every read and write tool. If a user at 
\f1\fs26 acme-001
\f0\fs24  asks about 
\f1\fs26 globex-001
\f0\fs24  or device 
\f1\fs26 DARFCP0BQM2G
\f0\fs24 , the query deterministically returns zero rows and triggers a cross-tenant refusal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 2. Planner + Analyst Loop (Agent Design \'97 25% & Grounding \'97 20%)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Planner Node:
\f0\b0  Outputs a structured 
\f1\fs26 ExecutionPlan
\f0\fs24  (list of concrete steps + intent classification: 
\f1\fs26 qa
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 trend_insight
\f0\fs24 , or 
\f1\fs26 action_request
\f0\fs24 ). This satisfies the explicit 
\f2\b Planning
\f0\b0  requirement and makes reasoning transparent in logs/README.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Analyst Node (Tool-Calling Loop):
\f0\b0  Uses purposeful, high-signal tools rather than raw arbitrary SQL alone:\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f1\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f5 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 query_fleet_snapshot(...)
\f0\fs24 : Current/filtered state of devices, OS versions, compliance, and software.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f1\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	
\f5 \uc0\u9702 
\f1 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 analyze_time_series_trends(...)
\f0\fs24 : Pre-built statistical/window-function queries for the 4 core trends in the dataset:\
\pard\tx1660\tx2160\pardeftab720\li2160\fi-2160\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl2
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Battery end-of-life:
\f0\b0  
\f1\fs26 cycle_count > 900
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 condition == 'Service Recommended'
\f0\fs24 , or declining 
\f1\fs26 full_charge_capacity
\f0\fs24  (
\f1\fs26 7VP16KHV88LM
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 8NM23J95R5I6
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 M4XVHUV1MEPZ
\f0\fs24 ).\
\ls3\ilvl2
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sustained RAM constraint:
\f0\b0  High 
\f1\fs26 used_memory_bytes / total_memory_bytes
\f0\fs24  ratio across the 30-day window.\
\ls3\ilvl2
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Storage exhaustion / rapid burn:
\f0\b0  Low 
\f1\fs26 available_bytes
\f0\fs24  or steep negative slope (
\f1\fs26 RLD7WV7J82SH
\f0\fs24  at 5.1 GB, 
\f1\fs26 MT7PJB7N5LRE
\f0\fs24  at 10.2 GB, 
\f1\fs26 E4V0SB5I0MYU
\f0\fs24  at 12.2 GB, 
\f1\fs26 8NM23J95R5I6
\f0\fs24  dropping 150 GB).\
\ls3\ilvl2
\f2\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compliance drift & unauthorized software:
\f0\b0  
\f1\fs26 LAG()
\f0\fs24  transitions where 
\f1\fs26 screen_lock
\f0\fs24  flipped 
\f1\fs26 pass -> fail
\f0\fs24  (10 devices) or unapproved apps (
\f1\fs26 uTorrent
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 TeamViewer
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 CleanMyMac X
\f0\fs24 ) appeared mid-month.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f2\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Grounding Verifier Node:
\f0\b0  Checks that every claimed device ID and metric in the draft response exists in the tool outputs from the current run, attaching structured citations (
\f1\fs26 device_id
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 collected_at
\f0\fs24 , metric values). If a user demands an action (e.g., 
\f3\i "Replace all MacBooks at Initech"
\f0\i0 ) without supporting telemetry evidence, this node blocks the action transition and forces an evidence-insufficient refusal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 3. Action Tools, 
\f4\fs26 interrupt()
\f2\fs24  HITL & Audit Log (Action Quality & Guardrails \'97 20%)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b0 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Implement the exact four action tools from the assignment (
\f1\fs26 create_upgrade_order
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 open_remediation_ticket
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 flag_device_for_replacement
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 notify_employee
\f0\fs24 ) backed by a state store (
\f1\fs26 actions_audit.jsonl
\f0\fs24  or SQLite 
\f1\fs26 audit_log
\f0\fs24  table).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 When the agent proposes an action, it invokes LangGraph's 
\f1\fs26 interrupt(\{"proposed_actions": [...], "evidence": [...]\})
\f0\fs24 . Execution halts cleanly until the caller resumes the graph with 
\f1\fs26 Command(resume=\{"approved": True/False, "approver": "..."\})
\f0\fs24 .\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Every proposal, approval, rejection, and refusal is written to the 
\f2\b Audit Log
\f0\b0  with timestamp, 
\f1\fs26 tenant_id
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 approver
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 tool_name
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 args
\f0\fs24 , 
\f1\fs26 evidence_refs
\f0\fs24 , and 
\f1\fs26 status
\f0\fs24 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

